The files under raw/ are WorldPop's own GeoTIFFs, byte for byte: each was
compared with the sha256 recorded for it in scripts/REFERENCE.json of the
source repository.

The files under cog/ were made from them and are changed in form only: the
same raster written as a Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF (DEFLATE compression with a
predictor, 512 by 512 tiles, overviews; nearest-neighbour overviews for the
degree of urbanisation, whose values are class codes). Every value at full
resolution was compared with the original and is equal; the overviews are
new.

parquet/files.parquet is a list of the files with their sizes, checksums and
the count and sum of their valid pixels, computed from the originals.

The code that fetches, checks and converts is MIT, in the repository this
dataset was built from (https://github.com/yuiseki/worldpop-jp-2026-01),
and does not apply here.
